---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How WizardLoop handles local preferences, GitHub Pages hosting and direct conversations by Telegram or email."
>
  <section class="wrap prose-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR BROWSER, YOUR CHOICE</p>
      <h1>
        Your privacy,
        <br />
        in plain language.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Updated <time datetime="2026-10-28">28 October 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>A small, static website</h2>
      <p>
        This is WizardLoop's personal creative website, hosted on GitHub Pages.
        The site does not run advertising, visitor analytics, contact forms or
        embedded social feeds. Fonts, illustrations and profile artwork are
        served with the site. No profile or post synchronization runs in the
        background.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub processes connection information to deliver and protect the
        website. Hosting can involve technical records such as IP addresses and
        browser details. Read the{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub Privacy Statement
        </a>{' '}
        for its practices.
      </p>
      <h2>Your appearance preferences</h2>
      <p>
        Your browser can remember your light or dark theme and whether you
        paused motion. These choices stay in local storage and are not sent to
        an analytics service. You can change them in the header or clear this
        website's data in your browser. See{' '}
        <a href="/cookies/">Cookies &amp; storage</a> for details.
      </p>
      <h2>Links and direct conversations</h2>
      <p>
        Telegram posts and GitHub repositories open on their original websites
        when you follow a link. This website does not load their widgets. Those
        services have their own privacy practices, including the{' '}
        <a href="https://telegram.org/privacy">Telegram Privacy Policy</a> and
        GitHub's policy linked above.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contact me by Telegram or email, I receive the information you
        choose to send and the account details your provider shares with the
        conversation. I use that information to understand your request and
        reply. There is no website submission service, CAPTCHA or separate
        feedback database. Your messaging or email provider also processes the
        conversation.
      </p>
      <h2>Keeping and deleting messages</h2>
      <p>
        Direct correspondence remains in the relevant mailbox or conversation
        until deleted. There is no automatic deletion schedule. I review
        deletion requests and retain information only where it remains needed
        for the conversation or an applicable legal obligation. Provider records
        and backups follow the provider's own policies; immediate deletion from
        independent provider systems cannot be promised.
      </p>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can browse without contacting me, clear local preferences, and ask
        about information you have sent. Where applicable law grants access,
        correction, deletion or other data-protection rights, contact me to make
        a request. Include enough context to locate the conversation without
        sending unrelated personal information. You may also contact the
        relevant data-protection authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, use <a href="/feedback/">the contact page</a>,
        email <a href="mailto:wizard@wizardloop.com">wizard@wizardloop.com</a>{' '}
        or <a href="https://t.me/wizardloop">message me on Telegram</a>. This
        notice describes the website's current behavior; it is not a
        certification of legal compliance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
